+name: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy
+def: "Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the TSEN2 gene. This condition is characterized by variable intellectual disability, growth delay, hypotonia, motor delay, ataxia, vision abnormalities, brain structural anomalies, and may include cardiac and pulmonary complications, proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and severe hypertension." [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/, PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994, PMID:32404165, PMID:34964109, PMID:38347586, PMID:38438125, PMID:38622473]
